title: Gnomon must run on Windows too; voice decisions
summary: 'Voice research landed (research 19, 20). Founder decisions: push-to-talk plus an opt-in conversation mode with barge-in; local-only voice in 8.0; a compacted lore record plus raw turns for the team chat log. New cross-cutting requirement: everything Gnomon builds must also work on Windows, which reopens the voice client build and every macOS-specific choice in the spec (sandbox-exec, Keychain, unix socket, MLX, CoreML).'
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-harness'
decisions:
  - id: P8-R4
    decision: 'Requirement: everything Gnomon builds must also work on Windows'
    rationale: 'Founder: "all of what we build needs to also work if on a windows"'
  - id: P8-D28
    decision: 'Voice interaction: push-to-talk by default plus a toggleable conversation mode with barge-in; mic state always visible'
    rationale: Safe default with a real back-and-forth when wanted.
  - id: P8-D29
    decision: Voice is local only in 8.0; only text goes to Claude; cloud speech-to-speech considered for 8.1
    rationale: Privacy; no official Anthropic realtime audio API.
  - id: P8-D30
    decision: 'Team chat log: every voice turn is a kernel event (text_planned vs text_spoken); at session end turns compact into a lore record linked to raw turns; shared text-only, redacted, with per-speaker consent; audio not kept by default'
    rationale: Lore-like log for teams without leaking audio.
learnings:
  - 'Windows support reopens macOS-specific choices: sandbox-exec (Windows needs AppContainer/job objects or an ACL backend, as deepseek-harness has), Keychain/Touch ID (Windows Credential Manager/Windows Hello), unix sockets (named pipes), MLX/CoreML/FluidAudio (Mac-only; need cross-platform engines with Mac acceleration as an optional backend).'
tags:
  - paradigm-8
